# --- AHC-inference: run artefacts ------------------------------------------
# run_inference.py writes everything under outputs/ (trajdump.npy, hparams.yaml,
# overall_factor.txt, the energy files and the observable cache) and copies the
# selected checkpoint to checkpoint.pkl. run_and_plot_observables.py drops its
# figures in the example directory itself. None of this is input.
examples/AHC-inference/outputs/
examples/AHC-inference/checkpoint.pkl
examples/AHC-inference/plot_*.pdf

# --- AHC-inference: bulk data ----------------------------------------------
# The Ne=16 checkpoints with their HF inputs (15 files, ~100 MB) and the dummy
# example (~5 MB) are tracked, so a fresh clone can run every row of
# simulations.csv. The Ne=36 set (~730 MB) is distributed separately -- ignore
# it if it is unpacked into checkpoints/ here.
examples/AHC-inference/checkpoints/*_ne36.pkl
examples/AHC-inference/checkpoints/*_ne36.h5
